{
  "name": "love-font",
  "height": 8,
  "spacing": 1,
  "legend": { "on": "#", "off": "." },
  "notes": [
    "Single source of truth for glyphs. build_font.py compiles this into BOTH",
    "src/font_love.h (firmware) and web/js/font.js (browser preview), so the",
    "on-screen preview is pixel-identical to the real matrix.",
    "",
    "Every glyph is exactly 8 rows. Width is inferred from the row length and",
    "may differ per glyph (proportional font). Row budget:",
    "  row 0     diacritic marks for UPPERCASE (kreska, kropka)",
    "  row 1     diacritic marks for lowercase",
    "  rows 0-6  glyph body, baseline at row 6",
    "  row 7     descenders (g j p q y) and the ogonek (a-ogonek, e-ogonek)",
    "",
    "Uppercase letters carrying a diacritic are compressed into rows 1-6 to",
    "make room for the mark on row 0. One pixel shorter is invisible at this",
    "size and is what real 8px fonts do.",
    "",
    "U+FFFD is the .notdef glyph, shown for any character with no entry."
  ],

